 can relate to  the way they drive the things that they  do and it actually makes the narrative  all about you all about your friends  which i think is much more compelling  and if it's turn 10 community manager  Brian Ekberg I know that character is  gonna drive like a total maniac and it's  totally gonna cut me off at the most  inopportune moments of a critical race  absolutely and you know what's really  cool for me about Drive attire is the  way an element of racing games which  maybe hasn't moved on for very for many  years suddenly is something you talk  about outside the game right you and  Brian will talk about the things that  his drivers are dead or your driver tart  that the same thing happens to me people  tweet me about the things my driver  tires doing in races in Forza 5 I think  we're gonna find that with horizon 2 you  know these these are events become water  cooler moments so we had a question here  about the soundtrack I forget who that  was but music you know the whole  festival was obviously a pretty big  party there is  Oh game yeah did just the vibe of the  overall soundtrack and the and the  licensed song does that change with the  setting moving from Colorado to Southern  Europe or is it kind of the overall tone  gonna stay the same so we're excited  about the music in horizon 2 I think we  did a great job in the first one more  people tweet me about the soundtrack and  horizon 1 than about any other aspect of  the game so our strategy for this game  is just to keep doing it more and more  right so the guy who created the  soundtrack in the first one robbed a  bank he's this English DJ festival  organizer he's back on board he's  curated the soundtrack for horizon 2 and  we've just given him more room to  express himself so we have twice as many  radio stations more than double the  amount of music on desk so we're  actually bringing you more and more  music more diversity we really hope that  you're gonna find songs you love but  you're also gonna fall in love with new  music as well so there's this moment  that we just saw in the footage here and  it's about 30 seconds past but you're  driving along the road and you're a  green driving line all of a sudden cuts  to the left and into this big open field  I don't know it's maybe a vineyard or  something like that but basically it's  one of those moments where I was playing  for the first time I was like wait this  can't be right this can't be right what  am i doing I can barely see I'm in a cog  for that view what's going on here I'm  just smashing into hay bales but it  seems like you know getting off the road  and kind of taking advantage of the  openness of an open world it's kind of a  focus for you guys right absolutely  absolutely we wanted to create a truly  open world this time you know we've  taken the view that if there are if  there aren't walls or barriers in real  life well there shouldn't be then  barriers are wolves in our game right we  want you to be able to drive on the road  we want you to be able to explore  anywhere off the road as well so what  you're talking about driving through a  vineyard we're in southern Tuscany here  so there's loss of any yards there are  across crop fields through forests  silver hills it's a whole new dimension  to exploration and driving with a  horizon too what it means is we've  actually got so much more space to fill  with cool stuff to do in cars right I'm  talking about races I'm talking about  non recent game plays well challenges  secrets and things to discover now how  do you balance those  sort of like crazy detours with the fact  that quite often you're gonna be driving  a McLaren p1 or a really really fancy  sports car that was designed to be  driven on the road yeah absolutely so  throughout the game I think there's a  there's a risk/reward thing going on  there right depending on the car you're  in sometimes it could be faster to stay  on the tarmac you know if you're in a  really high speed performance car  sometimes though if you're in an  off-roader a Ford Raptor or some of the  really extreme cars we've got in the  game it will pay to go off-road but  ultimately horizon the hope the whole  all-out franchise is about having fun  doing things which maybe aren't things  you would do in real life but things  which are just crazy fun and sometimes  driving across farmlands you know  through crop fields and a Lamborghini  Huracan it's just crazy fun and we  wanted to encourage you to do that and  we've got about a minute or two left  here but I would be just absolutely  trounced by our hardcore racing fans in  the audience if I didn't talk to you on  some level about just you know the  physics of the driving model obviously  your connection to Forza Motorsport  lends itself to any number of questions  about the simulation nature of what  you're trying to go for here the  original game you had all but a whole  bunch of driving assist that you could  toggle on to make the game pretty  hardcore but at the same time you you  didn't drill down into the really  esoteric stuff gear ratios and all that  what's your approach this time around so  a couple of things here so we start from  the starting point of having parts of  motorsport 5s engine that's where we  started from with all commented that  we've enhanced it in lots of different  ways but at its core we have that same  physics system phase physics simulation  that you seen for us a five it still  runs at three hundred and sixty Hertz  you know so there's incredible  complexity and sophistication and that  physics emulation a couple of things we  do first of all because we're driving in  an open world and the way you drive in  an open world is different from how you  drag on Laguna Seca or Nurburgring right  so I guess we rear-end off the edges of  some of the difficulty in that  simulation while still having the  complexity underlying it but we've  listened to our fans from the first game  a lot of guys said hey I want to tune my  car I want to be able to play with the  suspension with the gear ratios so we  brought that back before it's horizon to  horizon - you can upgrade your car  cosmetically in terms of engine parts  but you can also tune it in exactly the  same way you would import some  motorsport 5 so I I hope people are  going to be excited to experiment with  that  in September all right Ralph sounds  great I had a lot of fun playing it the  other night I'm probably going to try to  sneak over there again at some point -  be my guest all right thanks a lot for  joining us on the stage thanks Sean
 

